#: intro/faq.md:block 1 (header)
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr "常见问题"

#: intro/faq.md:block 2 (header)
msgid "Usage"
msgstr "使用"

#: intro/faq.md:block 3 (header)
msgid "Can Ceno Browser replace my current browser (Chrome/Firefox/Safari)?"
msgstr "Ceno 浏览器能否代替我现在的浏览器 (Chrome/Firefox/Safari)？"

#: intro/faq.md:block 4 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: yes, at least for some non-critical browsing."
msgstr "简而言之：可以，至少对于一些非关键性的浏览来说是这样。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 5 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Since Ceno is based on Mozilla Firefox for Android, it provides all the "
"features that are expected from a modern browser. However, its reliance on "
"Ouinet technology for retrieving web content may affect its operation in "
"subtle ways (some of them potentially involving your privacy)."
msgstr ""
"由于 Ceno 基于 Mozilla Firefox for "
"Android，它提供了现代浏览器的所有功能。但是，它依赖 Ouinet "
"技术来检索网络内容，这可能会以微妙的方式影响它的操作(其中一些可能涉及您的隐私"
")。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 6 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Also, since Ceno and Ouinet are under continuous development, you may "
"experience some instability. That may also mean that backwards-incompatible "
"changes are introduced which require you to uninstall the application or "
"remove stored data (including bookmarks and site settings) before upgrading."
msgstr ""
"此外，由于 Ceno 和 Ouinet "
"正在持续开发中，您可能会遇到一些不稳定的情况。这也可能意味着引入了向后不兼容"
"的更改，要求您在升级之前卸载应用程序或删除存储的数据（包括书签和站点设置）。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 7 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"For important work on Web sites not subject to censorship, we recommend that "
"you use your habitual Web browser instead of Ceno. Please read the section "
"on [risks](../concepts/risks.md) for more information."
msgstr ""
"对于不受审查的网站上的重要工作，我们建议您使用您习惯的浏览器，而不是 "
"Ceno。请阅读[风险](../concepts/risks.md)一节，了解更多信息。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 8 (header)
msgid "Can I use Ceno Browser to access Twitter, Facebook and Gmail?"
msgstr "我可以使用 Ceno 浏览器访问 Twitter、Facebook 和 Gmail 吗？"

#: intro/faq.md:block 9 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: yes, by using Personal tabs."
msgstr "简而言之：是的，通过使用个人标签页。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 10 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Although Ceno strives to provide a user experience as similar to normal Web "
"browsing as possible, some of the techniques used to avoid network "
"interference do not play well with such dynamic sites. This is the case with "
"Ceno's default mode of operation (i.e. public browsing), since it strips "
"down all private data (like passwords and cookies) from Web traffic to "
"ensure that it does not leak to other untrusted Ceno or Ouinet users."
msgstr ""
"尽管 Ceno "
"努力提供尽可能类似于正常网页浏览的用户体验，但一些用于避免网络干扰的技术并不"
"适用于这种动态网站。Ceno "
"的默认操作模式（即公共浏览）就是这种情况，因为它从网络流量中剥离所有私人数据"
"（如密码和 Cookies ），以确保不会泄露给其他不受信任的 Ceno 或 Ouinet 用户。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 11 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"To avoid this and enable the use of such dynamic sites in Ceno, you can use "
"Personal tabs (i.e. private browsing), which leave private data intact and "
"keep connections to the sites encrypted and thus protected from everyone "
"else. However, this requires that network traffic from your device can reach "
"those websites in some way."
msgstr ""
"为了避免这种情况，并允许在 Ceno "
"中使用这种动态网站，您可以使用个人标签页（即个人浏览），这样可以保持私人数据"
"完整，并保持与网站的加密连接，从而防止其他任何人访问。但是，这要求您设备的网"
"络流量能够以某种方式到达这些网站。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 12 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"For further details, please refer to the section on the differences between "
"[Public and Personal browsing](../concepts/public-personal.md)."
msgstr "有关更多详细信息，请参阅[公共浏览和个人浏览](../concepts/public-"
"personal.md)。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 13 (header)
msgid "Privacy and security"
msgstr "隐私和安全"

#: intro/faq.md:block 14 (header)
msgid "Will my device store content that I did not request?"
msgstr "我的设备会存储我没有请求的内容吗？"

#: intro/faq.md:block 15 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: no."
msgstr "简而言之：不会。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 16 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Ceno only shares content that you requested (using [Public browsing](../"
"concepts/public-personal.md))."
msgstr "Ceno 仅共享您使用[公共浏览](../concepts/public-personal.md)请求的内容。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 17 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Please note that a malicious website may still try to trick your browser "
"into retrieving content from other sites without your knowledge so as to "
"force your device to store and share it with other users. While Firefox code "
"already does a pretty good job at detecting and blocking such attempts, you "
"should still avoid visiting suspicious sites."
msgstr ""
"请注意，恶意网站仍可能试图在您不知情的情况下，诱使您的浏览器从其他网站检索内"
"容，从而迫使您的设备存储内容并与其他用户共享。虽然 Firefox "
"代码在检测和阻止这种尝试方面已经做得很好了，但是您仍然应该避免访问可疑的网站"
"。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 18 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Read more about how your Ceno Browser retrieves and shares Web content with "
"others [here](../concepts/how.md)."
msgstr "[点击此处](../concepts/how.md)了解更多关于 Ceno "
"浏览器如何检索网页内容并与其他人分享的信息。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 19 (header)
msgid "Can anyone see if I am using Ceno Browser to access censored Web sites?"
msgstr "有人能知道我是否在使用 Ceno 浏览器访问被审查的网站吗？"

#: intro/faq.md:block 20 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: yes, with some technical knowledge and resources."
msgstr "简而言之：是的，具备一定的技术知识和资源的话。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 21 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Ceno is not an anonymity tool. An attacker able to spy on your network "
"traffic can see content being requested from or served to another user from "
"your device. The attacker can also assess whether you are sharing a "
"particular website, although they cannot list all the content that you are "
"sharing."
msgstr ""
"Ceno "
"并非匿名工具。能够监视你网络流量的攻击者，可以看到从你的设备向其他用户请求的"
"内容或向其他用户提供的内容。攻击者还能判断你是否在分享某个特定网站，尽管他们"
"无法列出你正在分享的所有内容。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 22 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"However, content being retrieved into the network for the first time or "
"using [Personal browsing](../concepts/public-personal.md) will travel over "
"encrypted connections. See [how content retrieval works](../concepts/how.md) "
"and the associated [risks](../concepts/risks.md) for more information."
msgstr ""
"不过，首次接入网络的内容或使用[个人浏览](../concepts/public-"
"personal.md)的内容，将通过加密连接传输。有关更多信息，请参阅[内容检索原理]("
"../concepts/how.md)及相关的[风险](../concepts/risks.md)。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 23 (header)
msgid "Resource usage"
msgstr "资源使用"

#: intro/faq.md:block 24 (header)
msgid "Does Ceno Browser use a lot of data?"
msgstr "Ceno 浏览器会使用大量数据吗？"

#: intro/faq.md:block 25 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: more than your usual browser."
msgstr "简而言之：比你平时用的浏览器多。"

#: intro/faq.md:block 26 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Whenever your Ceno Browser serves content to another user or forwards their "
"traffic, it is consuming extra data depending on factors like how popular or "
"large the content is, and how well-connected your device is. Sharing more "
"content also implies more overhead."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 27 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Although Ceno is much lighter in resources than other data-sharing "
"applications, it can still result in increased data usage and fees. We "
"recommend keeping an eye on the app's data usage (under Android settings) "
"and running Ceno while connected to Wi-Fi instead of using mobile data."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 28 (header)
msgid "Does Ceno Browser use a lot of battery on my device?"
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 30 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Ceno and Ouinet use various techniques for different users to cooperate in "
"avoiding network interference and outages. Serving content to and forwarding "
"traffic for other users consumes extra power. Also, even when your device is "
"not actively helping other users, it still needs to stay reachable over the "
"network, which prevents the use of some energy-saving features."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 31 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"The net result is that Ceno may keep on draining your battery even when not "
"in use. Our tests have not shown power consumption hiking too much, but your "
"mileage may vary. When in need of battery, we recommend stopping Ceno "
"completely (it offers a convenient shortcut for this, see [here](../browser/"
"install.md))."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 32 (header)
msgid "Do I need to be connected to Wi-Fi to use Ceno Browser?"
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 33 (paragraph)
msgid "Short answer: no, but we strongly recommend it."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 34 (paragraph)
msgid ""
"Although Ceno should work fine on a mobile connection, there are two reasons "
"why we recommend using a Wi-Fi connection instead:"
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 35 (ordered list)
msgid ""
"Ceno consumes an extra amount of data which may result in a higher phone "
"bill (see above)."
msgstr ""

#: intro/faq.md:block 35 (ordered list)
msgid ""
"Mobile connections often make reaching your device more difficult from the "
"outside than Wi-Fi ones, thus decreasing the chances that you can help other "
"users get content."
msgstr ""
